# SyncScape — Product Flow & Feature Specification

---

## Overview

SyncScape is a dual-sided web application serving two user types:
- **Tenant** — A student/renter looking for a room and/or a compatible roommate.
- **Landlord** — A property owner listing accommodation.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **City-scoped only.** The platform is currently scoped to a Cork. All house listings and tenant-roommate matching happens within Cork; no cross-city features are needed at this stage.

---

## Step 1 — Sign Up (General / Common)

Both user types share the same registration screen.

| Field | Notes |
|---|---|
| Full Name | Required |
| Email | Required; used as display contact by default |
| Phone Number | Required; user can toggle visibility to matches |
| Password | Standard |
| User Type | `Tenant` or `Landlord` (radio/toggle) |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Phone number visibility is a **user-controlled toggle** — once toggled on, it is shown alongside the email on the user's match card instead of, or in addition to, the email so that your matches can view it.

After registration → **Log In** screen.

---

## Step 2 — Log In

Standard email + password login. On first login, the user is redirected to **Profile Setup** (Step 3). On subsequent logins, they go directly to the **Dashboard** (Step 4).

---

## Step 3 — Profile / Onboarding Setup

> **All sections below must be completed before the user can access the Dashboard.** Partial completion is saved as draft but does not unlock the dashboard.

### 3A — Landlord Onboarding: Create a Listing

A landlord must have **at least one active listing** to proceed. The creation flow has three sections:

#### Section 1 — Property Details
*(Fields defined in the onboarding flow file — refer to that file for the full field list)*
- Property name / title
- Location / address
- Rent (monthly)
- Room type (single, double, en-suite, etc.)
- Available from (date)
- Number of available rooms

#### Section 2 — Amenities
Checklist of offered amenities (e.g., WiFi, Washing Machine, Study Desk, Double Bed, Kitchen Access, etc.)

> [!NOTE]
> Each checked amenity becomes a verification target for the **VLM Listing Verification** pipeline (AI checks uploaded photos to confirm claims are visually supported).

#### Section 3 — Rules
- Pet policy
- Smoking policy
- Guest policy
- Quiet hours
- Any additional rules

#### Photos Upload
- Minimum 1 photo required; multiple encouraged.
- Photos are processed by the VLM pipeline in the background to:
  1. Cross-verify amenities claimed.
  2. Check photo quality (lighting, clarity).
- Listing is granted a **"Verified"** badge once VLM passes both checks.

