## Step 4 — Dashboard

The dashboard has a **top navigation header** with four tabs:

```
[ Houses ]  [ Roommate ]  [ Matches ]  [ Profile ]
```

---

### Tab 1 — Houses

A ranked grid of property listings, personalized to the tenant's preferences (Section 1 of onboarding).

**Grid Layout:**
- Top-left card = highest match score (most compatible listing).
- Remaining cards sorted by descending match score.
- Ranking is computed internally by the **Cosine Similarity / Two-Tower matching engine**.

**Each House Card displays:**
- **Photo section**: Large hero/main photo + small grid of additional photos. Bottom-right corner shows a **`+X` button** (e.g., `+4`) indicating how many more photos exist — clicking expands the full gallery.
- **Property name**
- **Location**
- **Two action buttons:**
  - ❤️ **Like** — saves/likes the property.
  - 🔗 **Share** — share with a matched roommate.
- **Like counter** — shows which people from your **matches list** have also liked this property (only visible within match context).

**House Detail View (on click):**
Full-page profile for the property containing:
- Full photo gallery
- Rent
- Full amenities list
- Rules
- Location map (if implemented)
- Verified badge (if VLM-approved)
- Landlord contact (after liking / mutual interest)

---

### Tab 2 — Roommate *(Tinder-style Swipe)*

The core feature. Shows potential roommate profiles ranked by compatibility score (based on matching lifestyle + accommodation preferences).

**Swipe Card contains:**
- Profile photo
- Name
- Age / University (if provided)
- Budget range
- Preferred area
- Lifestyle tags (e.g., "Night owl", "Pet-friendly", "Clean freak")
- **3 Personality Prompt answers** (from Section 3 of onboarding)
- Scroll down for full details within the card

**Interaction (Web version):**
- **← Arrow / Left click** = Swipe Left (skip / not interested)
- **→ Arrow / Right click** = Swipe Right (interested / want to room together)

**Matching logic:**
- A **Match** is created only when **both** tenants swipe right on each other (mutual swipe).
- If User A swipes right on User B but User B has not swiped yet, User A's profile appears in User B's **Likes tab**. User B can click into User A's profile from the Likes tab and then swipe to accept or decline — creating a match if they swipe right.
- Swiping left = skipped for now (profile not surfaced again by default).

---

---

### Tab 3 — Matches

Two sub-sections:

#### Matches
- Shows all **mutual matches** (both parties swiped right on each other).
- Each match is displayed as a **card** containing:
  - Profile photo
  - Name
  - Email (shown by default)
  - Phone number *(only if the matched user toggled this on)*
- Clicking a match card → opens the **Match Entity Dialog** (see below).

#### The Match Entity (Dialog/Overlay)
When you click on a match card, an overlay/dialog opens. This is the shared space between the two matched tenants. It contains:
- **Your matched person's profile info** — photo, name, contact details.
- **Shared Houses list** — all houses either party has shared with the other (see House Sharing below).

For each shared house in the dialog:
- The **receiver** of the shared house sees two action buttons:
  - ❤️ **Like** — marks the house as liked on their end.
  - ✅ **Apply** — signals they are willing to apply to rent this house with the matched person.
- The **sender** can see whether the other person has applied.
- **Both parties must click Apply** for the joint application to be submitted to the landlord.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> A joint application (pair application) is only submitted to the landlord once **both matched tenants have clicked Apply** on the same house. This confirms mutual intent to rent together.

#### House Sharing Flow
1. Tenant A is on the **Houses tab** and clicks the 🔗 **Share** button on a house card.
2. A picker shows their list of matches. Tenant A selects a match.
3. That house is added to the **Match Entity Dialog** between Tenant A and the selected match.
4. Tenant B (the match) sees the shared house in their Match Entity Dialog and can Like or Apply.

> [!NOTE]
> Sharing is **restricted to existing matches only** — you cannot share a house with someone who is not yet a mutual match.

#### Likes Sub-section
- Shows profiles of people who have **swiped right on you** but you haven't responded to yet.
- Each card shows:
  - Profile photo
  - Name only *(contact info hidden until mutual match)*
- Clicking a Likes card → opens their full **Roommate swipe-card profile** so you can swipe right (match) or left (skip).

> [!NOTE]
> Contact info is withheld in Likes to incentivize the swipe action and protect privacy before a mutual match is formed.

---

### Tab 4 — Profile

- View your own profile as others see it.
- Edit all onboarding sections (house preferences, lifestyle, prompts).
- Toggle email / phone number visibility.
- Account settings.

