## Landlord Dashboard

The landlord has a separate dashboard experience (not the same tabs as a tenant). It has two main sections:

### Section 1 — My Listings

A grid/list of all properties the landlord has created.

**Each listing card shows:**
- Main property photo
- Property name
- Address
- **Like count** — total number of tenant likes this listing has received.
  - Clicking the like count opens a **Likes Dialog** (overlay) that shows a list of the **names** of all tenants who have liked the property. No other info is shown (no contact details).

**Actions on listing card:**
- Edit listing
- Delete listing
- View full listing detail

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The landlord's **contact information is never displayed to tenants** at any point in the browsing flow. It is only shared after the landlord explicitly **Confirms** a pair application (see below).

---

### Section 2 — Applications (Match Applications)

This is the core workflow for the landlord. It shows all **joint pair applications** that have been submitted to any of their listings.

**How a pair application reaches here:**
- Two matched tenants both clicked **Apply** on the same shared house.
- This creates a joint application entity that appears in the landlord's Applications section for that listing.

**Application card shows:**
- The listing the pair applied for
- Tenant A's profile snapshot (photo + name)
- Tenant B's profile snapshot (photo + name)

**Landlord can click into the application** to view both tenants' full profiles (preferences, lifestyle, personality prompts).

**Two actions per application:**
| Action | Effect |
|---|---|
| ✅ **Confirm** | Application accepted. The landlord's contact details are shared with both tenants. The listing may be marked as pending/filled. |
| ❌ **Ignore** | Application rejected. The pair is removed from the landlord's applications list. |

> [!NOTE]
> Only after **Confirm** are the landlord's contact details revealed to the applying tenants. At no other point in the app is landlord contact info visible.

